## internal/server.go (or wherever the repo mounts modules)

Mount the new module the way existing modules are mounted:
{{- if .Module.GraphQL }}

```go
{{ .ModuleAlias }}Handler, err := {{ .ModuleAlias }}Graphql.Init()   // import {{ .ModuleAlias }}Graphql "{{ .ModuleImport }}/graphql"
if err != nil {
	return err
}
router.POST("/{{ .Module.Route }}", gin.WrapH({{ .ModuleAlias }}Handler))
router.GET("/{{ .Module.Route }}/playground", playgroundHandler("/{{ .Module.Route }}"))
```
{{- end }}
{{- if .Module.REST }}

```go
if err := {{ .ModuleAlias }}Rest.Init(router.Group("/{{ .Module.Route }}/v1")); err != nil {   // import {{ .ModuleAlias }}Rest "{{ .ModuleImport }}/rest"
	return err
}
```
{{- end }}

If the repo also serves routes under a gateway prefix (backend-a `withGatewayPrefix`, backend-b
`webhookPrefixes`), mount there too.
{{- if .Module.GraphQL }}

## Supergraph

- backend-b: add `{{ .Module.Route }}` to `scripts/supergraph/supergraph.yaml`
  (`routing_url: http://127.0.0.1:8080/{{ .Module.Route }}`); `scripts/supergraph/supergraph_test.go` fails until you do.
- backend-a: add it to `apollo-router/supergraph-local.yaml`.
- The deployed router lives in the GitOps repo (for backend-a `gitops-non-prod/apollo-router/values.yaml`,
  `routing_url: http://backend-a/{{ .Module.Route }}`). Do not edit that repo from here: hand the user this snippet.
{{- end }}

## Root docs

Add `{{ .Module.Name }}` to the module map in README.md and the Module Index in AGENTS.md (or the repo's
equivalents), one line each, linking `internal/app/{{ .Module.Name }}/README.md`.
